{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassEndomorphism.KzConnectionSl2","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassEndomorphism.KzConnectionSl2","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.MonoidAlgebra.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.Perm.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Logic.Equiv.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Abel","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.Perm.Fin","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Module","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.Deriv.Inv","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.Deriv.Mul"],"declarations":22,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZConnectionSl2.omegaAt_closed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZConnectionSl2.omegaAt_closed","kind":"theorem","line":326,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/kz-connection-sl2.lean#L326-L329","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZConnectionSl2.omegaAt_hasDerivAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZConnectionSl2.omegaAt_hasDerivAt","kind":"theorem","line":307,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/kz-connection-sl2.lean#L307-L324","doc":"**`d log(z_i − z_j)` is closed.** Along the line `t ↦ z + t u`, the function\n`t ↦ ω_{ij}(z + t u)(v)` has derivative `−(u_i − u_j)(v_i − v_j)/(z_i − z_j)²` at `0`,\nwhich is symmetric in `u` and `v`; so `dω_{ij}(u, v)`, the antisymmetrisation, is `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZConnectionSl2.kz_curvature_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZConnectionSl2.kz_curvature_zero","kind":"theorem","line":292,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/kz-connection-sl2.lean#L292-L299","doc":"**The KZ connection has zero curvature** (three points): `ω∧ω = 0` at every\nconfiguration with distinct coordinates, for all tangent vectors. Together with\n`omegaAt_closed` this is `dω − ω∧ω = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZConnectionSl2.relations_of_curvature_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZConnectionSl2.relations_of_curvature_zero","kind":"theorem","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/kz-connection-sl2.lean#L238-L290","doc":"**Converse: zero curvature forces the relations.** Pointwise the 2-forms on three\npoints span a line (translations act trivially), so one configuration gives one equation.\nTwo configurations, `z = (0, 1, 2)` and `z = (0, 1, 3)` with `u = e₀`, `v = e₁`, give\n`½C₁ + C₂ + ½C₃ = 0` and `⅓C₁ + ½C₂ + ⅙C₃ = 0` for the commutators\n`C₁ = [M₀₁, M₀₂]`, `C₂ = [M₀₁, M₁₂]`, `C₃ = [M₀₂, M₁₂]`, hence `C₁ + C₂ = 0` and\n`C₂ + C₃ = 0`: the three infinitesimal pure braid relations. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZConnectionSl2.omegaWedgeOmega_expand","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZConnectionSl2.omegaWedgeOmega_expand","kind":"theorem","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/kz-connection-sl2.lean#L224-L236","doc":"`ω∧ω` with no relations assumed: the three commutators, each weighted by a\nwedge of two of the scalar forms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZConnectionSl2.curvature_zero_of_isFlat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZConnectionSl2.curvature_zero_of_isFlat","kind":"theorem","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/kz-connection-sl2.lean#L205-L222","doc":"**The relations force zero curvature.** For symmetric residues satisfying the\ninfinitesimal pure braid relations, `(ω ∧ ω)(u, v) = 0` at every configuration with\ndistinct coordinates, for all tangent vectors `u, v`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZConnectionSl2.omegaWedgeOmega_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZConnectionSl2.omegaWedgeOmega_eq","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/kz-connection-sl2.lean#L187-L203","doc":"Expanding `ω∧ω` and using two of the braid relations leaves one commutator times\nthe left side of the Arnold relation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZConnectionSl2.omegaWedgeOmega","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZConnectionSl2.omegaWedgeOmega","kind":"def","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/kz-connection-sl2.lean#L183-L185","doc":"The quadratic part of the curvature, `(ω ∧ ω)(u, v)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZConnectionSl2.connForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZConnectionSl2.connForm","kind":"def","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/kz-connection-sl2.lean#L179-L181","doc":"The connection form `ω = M₀₁ ω₀₁ + M₀₂ ω₀₂ + M₁₂ ω₁₂` on the tangent vector `u`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZConnectionSl2.arnold","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZConnectionSl2.arnold","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/kz-connection-sl2.lean#L164-L175","doc":"**Arnold relation**, pointwise, at a configuration with distinct coordinates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZConnectionSl2.omegaAt_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZConnectionSl2.omegaAt_symm","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/kz-connection-sl2.lean#L161-L162","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZConnectionSl2.wedge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZConnectionSl2.wedge","kind":"def","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/kz-connection-sl2.lean#L158-L159","doc":"The wedge of two scalar 1-forms, evaluated on `(u, v)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZConnectionSl2.omegaAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZConnectionSl2.omegaAt","kind":"def","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/kz-connection-sl2.lean#L155-L156","doc":"`d log(z_i − z_j)` at the point `z`, evaluated on the tangent vector `u`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZConnectionSl2.not_isFlat_example","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZConnectionSl2.not_isFlat_example","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/kz-connection-sl2.lean#L118-L131","doc":"**The predicate has content**: a family of residues on three points that is not\nflat. Take `M₀₁ = s₀₁`, `M₀₂ = s₁₂` and every other residue `0`; then\n`M₀₁ (M₀₂ + M₁₂) = s₀₁ s₁₂ ≠ s₁₂ s₀₁ = (M₀₂ + M₁₂) M₀₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZConnectionSl2.kz_isFlat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZConnectionSl2.kz_isFlat","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/kz-connection-sl2.lean#L104-L116","doc":"**The `𝔰𝔩₂` KZ connection is flat**: its residues satisfy the infinitesimal pure\nbraid relations. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZConnectionSl2.commute_sub_scalar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZConnectionSl2.commute_sub_scalar","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/kz-connection-sl2.lean#L91-L100","doc":"Subtracting central scalars does not change whether two elements commute. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZConnectionSl2.swap_commute_disjoint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZConnectionSl2.swap_commute_disjoint","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/kz-connection-sl2.lean#L84-L89","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZConnectionSl2.swap_conj_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZConnectionSl2.swap_conj_right","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/kz-connection-sl2.lean#L78-L82","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZConnectionSl2.swap_conj_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZConnectionSl2.swap_conj_left","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/kz-connection-sl2.lean#L72-L76","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZConnectionSl2.IsFlatLogConnection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZConnectionSl2.IsFlatLogConnection","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/kz-connection-sl2.lean#L64-L70","doc":"**Flatness of a logarithmic connection** with residues `M`: the infinitesimal\npure braid relations. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZConnectionSl2.kzResidue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZConnectionSl2.kzResidue","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/kz-connection-sl2.lean#L58-L62","doc":"The KZ residue in slots `i, j`: the split Casimir `Ω_{ij} = s_{ij} − ½`. Here `half`\nis meant to be `2⁻¹`; nothing below uses that, since the scalar part is central and\ndrops out of every commutator. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:kz-connection-sl2","label":"def:kz-connection-sl2","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/kz-connection-sl2.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZConnectionSl2.SymAlg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZConnectionSl2.SymAlg","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/kz-connection-sl2.lean#L55-L56","doc":"The symmetric-group algebra `R[S_n]`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}